G. The WHO Safety Checklist should be observed as in any other surgical procedures."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1398"}}, {"id": "body-11999", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The Embryologist should immediately examine the aspirated fluid under microscope in theater to look for oocyte before transferring to the IVF Lab", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Embryologist"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immediately"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "examine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aspirated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fluid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "under"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "microscope"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "theater"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "look"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oocyte"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "before transferring to the IVF Lab"}]}, {"id": "body-12001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Fertilization and Embryo culture are done few hours after the egg retrieval using the culture media and incubator in a tightly controlled IVF laboratory.", "runs": [{"text": "Fertilization and Embryo culture ", "bold": true}, {"text": "are done few hours after the egg retrieval using the culture media and incubator in a tightly controlled IVF laboratory."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1398"}}, {"id": "body-12002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The embryologist should monitor the process of fertilization, embryos development and grading them according to how the develop at each stage", "runs": [{"text": "The embryologist should monitor the process of fertilization, embryos development and grading them according to how the develop at each stage"}]}, {"id": "body-12003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The husband/partner should produce the sample on the day of the egg retrieval. The sperm sample is best produced by masturbation. It is recommended that the husband/partner should abstain from intercourse (No ejaculation) for two days before the egg retrieval in order to give a good sperm sample.", "runs": [{"text": "The husband/partner should produce the sample on the day of the egg retrieval. The sperm sample is best produced by masturbation."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "husband/partner"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abstain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "intercourse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(No"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ejaculation)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "two"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "before the egg retrieval in order to give a good sperm sample."}]}, {"id": "body-12005", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Embryo Transfer done under trans abdominal Ultrasound and the patient should be advised to have a full bladder before the procedure. The fertility specialist and Embryologist should discuss with the patient/couple on the number of embryos to be transferred at once, based on the specific patient circumstances, age of the woman and quality & number of the embryos available.", "runs": [{"text": "Embryo Transfer ", "bold": true}, {"text": "done under trans abdominal Ultrasound and the patient should be advised to have a full bladder before the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "procedure."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fertility"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "specialist"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Embryologist"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discuss"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient/couple"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "number"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "embryos"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be transferred at once, based on the specific patient circumstances, age of the woman and quality & number of the embryos "}, {"text": "available."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1398"}}, {"id": "body-12006", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It should be noted that transferring more than one embryo carries the risks of multiple pregnancies (twins or triplets) which are serious. As globally most of ART units are moving towards single embryo transfer, it is recommended to consider transferring of single or two embryos", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "noted"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transferring"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "one"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "embryo"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "carries"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "multiple"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(twins"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "triplets)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are serious. As globally most of ART units are moving towards single embryo transfer, it is recommended to consider transferring of single or two embryos"}]}, {"id": "body-12008", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Luteal Phase Support achieved by supplementation of progesterone 400mg per vagina twice a day from the day of egg retrieval and continued depending on indications", "runs": [{"text": "Luteal Phase Support ", "bold": true}, {"text": "achieved by supplementation of progesterone 400m